# Root .dockerignore for the FLASHIda parent repo.
#
# WHEN THIS FILE IS READ
# ----------------------
# Docker reads `<context>/.dockerignore`, so this file applies ONLY to a build
# whose context is the repo root. The sanctioned builds use the per-OS subdir as
# the context (`docker build docker/linux`, `docker build docker/windows` -- the
# Dockerfile's `COPY entrypoint.sh` only resolves that way), and this
# file is not consulted for those at all.
#
# It exists as belt-and-braces for the day someone types `docker build .` here.
# That is not a hypothetical cost: the repo root is ~1.6 GB, `OpenMS/src` alone
# is 842 MB, and NEITHER image bakes in any repo source -- the repo reaches the
# containers through a bind mount, never through a COPY. So the correct context
# from the root is "essentially nothing", and this file makes that the default
# instead of a 1.6 GB accident that also happens to sweep up the decrypted
# Thermo DLLs.
#
# SEMANTICS: the LAST matching pattern wins. The deny-all comes first, the
# re-includes come after it, and the never-ship rules come after those so they
# cannot be re-enabled by a re-include.

# --- 1. Deny everything -------------------------------------------------------
# `*` covers top-level entries; `**` covers every depth. Both, deliberately:
# the classic builder and BuildKit have historically differed on which of the
# two they honour, and neither is expensive to state.
*
**

# --- 2. Re-include only the container support files ---------------------------
# `!docker` re-includes the DIRECTORY so the walker descends into it at all;
# `!docker/**` re-includes its contents. This is the whole allowlist: today the
# Dockerfiles COPY only their entrypoint (`COPY entrypoint.sh /entrypoint.sh`),
# and `docker/` also holds ci-lists.awk / ci-lists.sh, which a future COPY may
# want. Nothing outside `docker/` is ever a legitimate COPY source.
!docker
!docker/**

# --- 3. Never ship, under any pattern -----------------------------------------
# Listed after the re-includes so they win even if one of these ever lands
# inside `docker/`. Rules 1-2 already exclude the FlashIDA paths; these are
# stated by name so the intent survives an edit to the allowlist above.
#
# Thermo iAPI DLLs are proprietary, are decrypted host-side into
# FlashIDA/dependencies/ at run time, and must never enter an image layer.
**/dependencies/*.dll
**/dependencies/*.enc
FlashIDA/dependencies

# No secret may appear in a build context, a layer or a log line.
**/*.pem
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/secrets
**/*.secret

# Git metadata: 500+ MB of pack files and every credential a helper cached.
.git
.git/**
**/.git
**/.git/**

# Host-only state that would bust the build cache on every edit.
.claude
.superpowers
.golden-assessment
